# {{ .ProviderShortName }} Provider

Manage [KinD](https://kind.sigs.k8s.io/) (Kubernetes in Docker) clusters as
Terraform resources. The provider embeds kind's own Go library rather than
shelling out to the `kind` binary, so cluster creation, refresh and destroy are
driven directly by the same code the `kind` CLI uses.

Typical uses are ephemeral clusters for CI pipelines, reproducible local
development environments, and integration tests that need a real API server.

## Requirements

| Requirement | Notes |
| ----------- | ----- |
| [Docker](https://docs.docker.com/get-docker/) | Must be installed **and running**. Podman and nerdctl are auto-detected by kind but are not covered by this provider's test suite. |
| Terraform >= 1.0 | Or OpenTofu >= 1.6. |
| Disk and memory | Each node is a container. A three-node cluster needs roughly 4&nbsp;GB of RAM. |

The `kind` CLI itself is **not** required. Installing it anyway is useful for
troubleshooting, because `kind get clusters` and `kind export logs` inspect the
same clusters this provider manages.

