## Connecting to the Docker daemon

The provider talks to Docker through kind, which reads the standard `DOCKER_HOST`
environment variable. Set the `host` argument to override it for this provider
only — useful with Colima, Rancher Desktop, Docker in a VM, or a rootless daemon.

```terraform
provider "kind" {
  host = "unix:///Users/me/.colima/default/docker.sock"
}
```

Leaving `host` unset (or setting it to an empty string) leaves any existing
`DOCKER_HOST` untouched.

