## Using the cluster with other providers

`kind_cluster` exports the credentials the `kubernetes` and `helm` providers
need. The certificate attributes are base64-encoded exactly as they appear in a
kubeconfig, so decode them before use:

```terraform
provider "kubernetes" {
  host                   = kind_cluster.this.endpoint
  client_certificate     = base64decode(kind_cluster.this.client_certificate)
  client_key             = base64decode(kind_cluster.this.client_key)
  cluster_ca_certificate = base64decode(kind_cluster.this.cluster_ca_certificate)
}
```

A complete, runnable version of this pattern — including an ingress controller
installed with Helm — is in
[`examples/complete/kubernetes-provider`](https://github.com/elioseverojunior/terraform-provider-kind/tree/main/examples/complete/kubernetes-provider).

## Troubleshooting

### `Cannot connect to the Docker daemon`

Docker is not running, or is listening somewhere the provider is not looking.
Verify with `docker info`, then set the provider's `host` argument if your
daemon uses a non-default socket.

### Apply fails after `timeout ... waiting for nodes to become ready`

The cluster was created but one or more nodes never reached `Ready`. The error
names the nodes still pending. Inspect them with:

```shell
kubectl --context kind-<cluster-name> describe node <node-name>
```

The usual causes are insufficient memory allocated to Docker, or a
`disable_default_cni = true` cluster with no replacement CNI installed. Raise
`wait_for_ready` for slow machines, or set `wait_for_nodes_ready = false` to
return as soon as the control plane responds.

### A cluster is replaced on every plan

Almost every argument on `kind_cluster` is `RequiresReplace`, because kind
cannot reconfigure a running cluster. Check `terraform plan` output for which
attribute changed — a drifting `node_image` tag is the most common cause. Pin
it to an exact digest or version.

### Port already allocated

`extra_port_mappings` binds host ports. If another cluster or service already
holds the port, creation fails. Pick a different `host_port`, or set
`networking.api_server_port = 0` to let the kernel choose a free API port.
